# Manual test of the local server API with the VS Code extension "REST Client"
# (id humao.rest-client, install it from the Extensions view). It adds a "Send Request" link above
# every "###" block of this file; click it (or press Ctrl+Alt+R inside a block) and the answer opens
# in a pane on the right. Run the blocks in order, 1 to 9.
# Start the server without a browser, so the one-time link stays unused:
#
#   scripts/run.sh --no-browser
#
# The server prints a line like
#   Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/#token=<64 characters> in your browser (it works once, for 2 minutes).
# Put the 64 characters after "#token=" into the file tests/manual/api/.env (Git ignores it), as
#   TBR_LINK_TOKEN=<64 characters>
# The file local_api.env.example shows the format.

@port = 8080
@token = {{$dotenv TBR_LINK_TOKEN}}

### 1. The placeholder page (no login needed)
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/

### 2. Log in with the link token: 204 and a Set-Cookie header (a second try gives 401)
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/session
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"{{token}}"}

### 3. Am I logged in? 204 after step 2, 401 before it
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/session
X-TaxBroker: 1

### 4. Upload the synthetic pipeline files for 2024: 200 and the whole result (schema 2)
# The extension keeps the session cookie of step 2. The files are read from the repository next to
# this file. The result has runRevision 1 and one open request, the deposit interest total.
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk

--tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="request"
Content-Type: application/json

{"reportingYear":2024,"filingType":"original","developerMode":false,
 "taxpayer":{"taxNumber":"12345679","isResident":true,"name":"Synthetic Taxpayer"},
 "files":[{"part":"file0","kind":"broker","broker":"trade_republic"},
          {"part":"file1","kind":"broker","broker":"trade_republic"},
          {"part":"file2","kind":"ecb_rates"}]}
--tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file0"; filename="export_2023_2024.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../../test_data/pipeline/export_2023_2024.csv
--tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file1"; filename="export_2024_2025.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../../test_data/pipeline/export_2024_2025.csv
--tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file2"; filename="report_ecb_rates.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../../test_data/cli/report_ecb_rates.csv
--tbrBoundary7MA4YWxk--

### 5. The result again (404 {"error":"no_run"} before step 4)
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run
X-TaxBroker: 1

### 6. Answer the deposit question for revision 1: 200, runRevision 2
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run/answers
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{"runRevision":1,"answers":[{"requestId":"request-0001","answer":"above_limit"}]}

### 7. The same answer again: 422, answer_rejected.stale_revision, nothing changes
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run/answers
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{"runRevision":1,"answers":[{"requestId":"request-0001","answer":"above_limit"}]}

### 8. Download Doh-KDVP for revision 2: 200 and Doh-KDVP_2024.xml (revision=1 gives 409)
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run/reports/capitalGains/xml?revision=2
X-TaxBroker: 1

### 9. Delete the recorded answer: 200, runRevision 3, the deposit question is open again
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/run/decisions/delete
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{"runRevision":2,"decisionIds":["decision-0001"]}
